<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65800" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελαινίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the black</i>, a name of Aphrodite at Corinth, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				13.588c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a bivalve
				<i>sea-shell</i>, used as a drinking-cup, <i><span class="en">
				Sophr.
				101
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				1.79
			</span></i>; 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελωρίς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Xenocr.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				2.58.97
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελαῖνις</span> (sic) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἲξ καὶ βοῦς</span>
			<i>from Melaenae</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diosc.Gloss.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.120
			</span></i>.</div>
